LC2 (#872): Build/Test/Deploy adapters for the dev pipeline

Original task: Wrap the four dev-pipeline operations (build / test /
preview deploy / production deploy) as governed code.tool agents in the
existing DomainAdapter pipeline. Production deploys must require admin
approval via a `dev-sensitive` policy profile. Build minutes flow into
execution_tasks.cost_usd.

What landed:
- Four DomainAdapters under
  supabase/functions/_shared/execution/adapters/{build,test,deploy/preview,deploy/prod}/
  with structured JSON logs (events `build.run.*`, `test.run.*`,
  `deploy.preview.*`, `deploy.prod.*`), and cost_usd / latency_ms
  surfaced on output for the orchestrator to persist.
- Real default runners:
  - build/deno-runner.ts spawns `vite build` via Deno.Command and
    walks dist/ for bundle size.
  - test/deno-runner.ts spawns `vitest --reporter=json` and parses
    pass/fail/skip + coverage (lines/statements/branches/functions
    pct) from the trailing JSON line, supporting both istanbul
    (`coverageMap.total`) and v8 (`coverage.summary.total`) shapes.
  - deploy/vercel-runner.ts posts to the Vercel REST `v13/deployments`
    endpoint, reading the access token only from the env var named in
    `metadata.router.primary.key_env` (default VERCEL_ACCESS_TOKEN).
  Each runner is overridable so tests inject deterministic stubs.
- deploy.prod adapter has defense-in-depth: refuses to call Vercel
  without `task.approved_by`, even though the orchestrator's
  authorization gate normally fires first. The deploy.prod verifier
  also refuses to ratify success without `approved_by` on the row
  (dev-sensitive policy hook).
- Verifiers for all four task types unwrap the orchestrator's
  `{output, logs, actions_taken}` payload and ratify shape + key
  fields.
- Migration `20260430000000_lc2_build_test_deploy_agents.sql` upserts
  the `dev-default` and `dev-sensitive` policy profiles and registers
  the four code.tool agents via `system.register_agent` (idempotent).
  No plain secrets — Vercel token is referenced via env-var
  indirection in agent metadata.
- All four bootstraps are wired into
  supabase/functions/execution-loop/index.ts alongside the marketplace
  + AI bootstraps, and follow the same fail-closed reconcile pattern
  (production = hard boot fail; dev/preview = log and continue).
- Integration test
  `src/__tests__/lc2-build-test-deploy.integration.test.ts` covers
  happy path + failures + defense-in-depth gate; 12/12 passing,
  no `any` casts (typed `executionOutput` / `costFields` helpers).

Deviations from the plan:
- rollback_strategy is "none" for all four adapters — builds, tests
  and deploys have no inverse in LC2 scope. LC6 may extend deploy.prod
  with a "promote previous" rollback handler.

Validation:
- vitest: 29/29 pass (LC2 + agent-registry suites green).
- tsc --noEmit: clean.

